---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import UnhurriedArchitecture from '../components/UnhurriedArchitecture.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Projects & Systems"
  description="Curated technical projects, cloud architecture blueprints, forensics investigations, and engineering research by Mohammad Ishfaque Jahan Rafee."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <h1 class="page-title">Projects &amp; Systems</h1>
    <p class="page-lead">
      A curated overview of my active systems engineering endeavors, cloud defense tooling, digital forensics investigations, and academic research.
    </p>
  </header>

  <!-- Featured Project: Unhurried -->
  <section id="unhurried" class="project-block">
    <div class="project-header">
      <div class="project-title-group">
        <span class="project-kicker">Flagship Systems Project</span>
        <h2 class="project-title">Unhurried — The Intentional Career Platform</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="project-meta-links">
        <a
          href="https://github.com/Unhurried-Careers"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="badge"
        >
          GitHub Organization ↗
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        AI auto-apply bots have flooded recruitment pipelines, creating noise for hiring teams and fatigue for job seekers. <strong>Unhurried</strong> takes the opposite approach: leveraging AI not as a spam cannon, but as a <strong>personal researcher</strong> that enables candidates to pursue a small, curated set of opportunities with genuine intent and tailored fit.
      </p>

      <h3>Core Design Principles</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Company Watchlists</strong>: Track specific companies with documented rationale before roles are broadly published, actively reading Greenhouse, Lever, and Ashby job boards.</li>
        <li><strong>Strict Shortlist Limit</strong>: Candidates are hard-capped at a maximum of <strong>5 active roles</strong> at any time. Moving a role to the shortlist requires written answers for <em>"Why this company?"</em> and <em>"Why this role?"</em>.</li>
        <li><strong>Intentional Outreach Kit</strong>: Generates personalized 300-character notes aimed at curious, peer-to-peer conversations rather than transactional referral requests.</li>
        <li><strong>Resume Studio</strong>: Deeply tailors a Google Doc resume to one shortlisted role based on selected skill focus areas.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Interactive Architecture Diagram -->
    <UnhurriedArchitecture />

    <div class="prose">
      <h3>Key Architecture Components</h3>

      <h4>1. Frontend Tier (<code>unhurried-web</code> &amp; <code>unhurried-extension</code>)</h4>
      <p>
        A Single Page Application built with <strong>React</strong> and <strong>TypeScript</strong>, hosted on <strong>Firebase Hosting</strong> for global low-latency CDN distribution. Accompanied by a dedicated <strong>Chrome Extension (Manifest V3)</strong> that integrates directly with job application portals to pull context and assist intentional submissions without mindless autofill.
      </p>

      <h4>2. Backend Microservices (<code>Go</code> on Google Cloud Run)</h4>
      <p>Five decoupled, single-responsibility services packaged in separate Git repositories:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong><code>unhurried-job-search</code></strong>: Polls and monitors external ATS boards (Greenhouse, Lever, Ashby) against user watchlists.</li>
        <li><strong><code>unhurried-applications</code></strong>: Enforces shortlist quotas (&le; 5), manages the outreach kit, and tracks conversation notes.</li>
        <li><strong><code>unhurried-resume</code></strong>: Tailoring service integrating Google Docs APIs.</li>
        <li><strong><code>unhurried-inbox</code></strong>: Read-only Gmail integration parsing incoming interview invites and proposing calendar slots.</li>
        <li><strong><code>unhurried-notifications</code></strong>: Asynchronous notification dispatch via email.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong><code>unhurried-common</code></strong> provides a shared Go foundational module standardizing HTTP hardening, token validation, logging, and common data models.
      </p>

      <h4>3. Zero-Trust Security &amp; Identity</h4>
      <p>
        <strong>Dual-Layer Authentication</strong> via Google Identity Platform and Firebase Auth. Google Cloud API Gateway validates incoming JWT ID tokens and API keys; downstream Go services cryptographically re-verify tokens, validate Firebase App Check attestations, and enforce tenant allowlists (<code>allowed_emails</code>).
      </p>

      <h4>4. Infrastructure as Code &amp; CI/CD (<code>unhurried-infra</code>)</h4>
      <p>
        100% codified using <strong>Terraform</strong> managing all Cloud Run instances, API Gateways, IAM bindings, and Firestore instances. A two-stage pipeline uses <strong>GitHub Actions</strong> for credential-free hermetic CI (linting, tests), while <strong>Google Cloud Build</strong> and <strong>Google Cloud Deploy</strong> handle staging and production rollouts with verified SLSA provenance into Artifact Registry.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="section-divider" />

  <!-- Cloud Security & Automation -->
  <section class="project-block">
    <div class="project-header">
      <div class="project-title-group">
        <span class="project-kicker">Cloud Security &amp; Defense</span>
        <h2 class="project-title">Enterprise Multi-Cloud Security Auditing &amp; IaC</h2>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Developed custom audit and verification tooling to enforce Cloud Security Posture Management (CSPM) and least-privilege Identity and Access Management (IAM) across hybrid enterprise cloud tenants spanning <strong>AWS</strong> and <strong>Oracle Cloud Infrastructure (OCI)</strong>. Automated the extraction and parsing of security configuration baselines using Python and Go, generating actionable remediation reports.
      </p>
      <p>
        Architected modular <strong>Terraform</strong> configurations to replace manual console deployments. Ensured disaster recovery environments and cloud workloads can be reliably recreated from declarative, version-controlled definitions with integrated security baselines.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="section-divider" />

  <!-- DFIR & Malware Analysis -->
  <section class="project-block">
    <div class="project-header">
      <div class="project-title-group">
        <span class="project-kicker">Digital Forensics &amp; Threat Intelligence</span>
        <h2 class="project-title">DFIR Memory Forensics &amp; Vulnerability Research</h2>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Authored in-depth forensic writeups and investigation walkthroughs for <strong>Hack The Box Sherlocks</strong> (including <em>Recollection</em>, <em>RogueOne</em>, and <em>Meerkat</em>) using Volatility 2 and Volatility 3:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Extracted injected DLLs, anomalous process hierarchies, dumped credentials, and command-and-control (C2) persistence mechanisms from full raw memory dumps.</li>
        <li>Traced network attack vectors, Suricata/Snort alert interpretation, and exploit payload tracing.</li>
        <li>Published technical analyses on zero-day, zero-click exploit chains (such as the 2023–2024 Apple iMessage hardware/software vulnerability chain documented by Kaspersky).</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="section-divider" />

  <!-- Academic Robotics -->
  <section class="project-block">
    <div class="project-header">
      <div class="project-title-group">
        <span class="project-kicker">Academic Research</span>
        <h2 class="project-title">Autonomous Robotics &amp; Power Electronics</h2>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>Co-authored peer-reviewed research papers published in IEEE Conference Proceedings:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Self-localization of a mobile robot using monocular vision of a chessboard pattern</strong>: Implemented a real-time self-localization framework for autonomous mobile robots using monocular camera input tracking planar chessboard pattern markers and perspective-n-point algorithms.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Modeling and simulation of a Microcontroller based power factor correction converter</strong>: Modeled and simulated a closed-loop digital control converter to optimize electrical efficiency and minimize harmonic distortion.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .project-block {
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  .project-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .project-kicker {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .project-title {
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
    font-size: 1.65rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }

  .section-divider {
    border: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    margin: 3rem 0;
  }
</style>
